While in nethack none of my characters that reached AC -14 ever died, I
have now already wasted the second Valkyrie in slashem that had an AC of
-15 or better!  In fact, this one had -35.  It was also my first
character to die in the quest.  The Valkyrie quest, of all possibilities
- one of the easiest ones!  Seven Valkyries in a row, none ascended -
makes Valks my worst class yet...  (but only in slashem :-) ).

She was a doppelganger, and she did not start out as promising as her
predecessor, Martha, who had stupidly stepped in a pool of lava in
Sokoban.  But there was an altar to Odin on Dlvl 1, so there was the
chance to get Mjollnir early.

She found a long sword soon, so she could ditch her spear.

In the town on Dlvl 5, she used a blessed scroll of identify in a shop
to identify a few unpaid items.  A wand of magic missile, a ring of
polymorph control, and a wand of enlightenment.  She bought the wand of
magic missile and did not have enough money left to buy the ring of
polycontrol.  With hindsight, it would have been better to buy the ring
first.

In the mines, she fell from level 5 through to level 9 and thought that
would be the end already.  But she managed to move back up again.
Minetown was on Dlvl 8 and did not yield anything remarkable, but since
she had telepathy from a floating eye on Dlvl 2 and a towel, she could
locate four killer bees in a room - a possible later source for poison
resistance, but not now - she did not have a unicorn horn yet.

On the way up, she met a statue gargoyle and found that she could not
harm it hitting it with her sword.  She used up all but two charges of
the wand of magic missile without being able to kill it.  Fortunately,
she could outrun it and lure it into a level teleport trap.  She met it
again on Dlvl 4 of the main dungeon and ran away again, leaving her pet
behind.  But now she had the 400 zorkmids for the ring of polycontrol
(and she was already level 8, so she almost did not need it anymore).

After buying it, she decided to become a dragon.  Green was the choice
of her color, for a reason.  Up she went, there was the gargoyle.  It
was gone after one bite.  Dragons have amazing attack powers in slashem.
She moved down to mine town.  Unfortunately, dragons cannot open doors,
but they can - strangely - kick them in.  No watchman in sight?  O.k.,
let's do it.  The four bees were no match, but only two left corpses.
Eating the first corpse, she just got the message: "Eech that must have
been poisonous... " but that she was not affected.  The second gave:
"You feel especially healthy".  Good!  A grey elf on the same level had
given her sleep resistance.

She then decided to do Sokoban first, hoping for the amulet, having a
bag of holding already.  On Dlvl 5, a fire ant provided fire resistance,
on Sokoban 2 a gelatinous cube shock resistance.  Later she would get
disintegration resistance from a tin of black dragon meat produced in
Ludios.

She solved all the puzzles in Sokoban despite her poor intelligence.
Only once did she blunder, having figured out the right sequence but
forgetting to move a boulder aside to be able to get behind it later.
But a doppelganger is not deterrable by a "you cannot pass this way". I
believe this was the only time, I used the liquify technique of a
doppelganger in this game.

Sokoban had the amulet indeed.

Then she decided to do the mines to the bottom, having also found a wand
of polymorph which allowed her to polymorph without losing energy.
Approaching the bottom she decided to become a lich, "increasing" her AC
from -10 to -24 temporarily.

The bottom was the one where the position of the luckstone is
predetermined on the right of the map;  there were a titan and a mind
flayer on the level, so obviously there was a polymorph trap someplace.
  She decided to polymorph into a black dragon and first disintegrated
the titan, which thereafter turned into a gnome, to be disposed of
easily.  Same thing for the mind flayer.  To get the luck stone, she had
to return to doppelganger form to be able to use her pick axe.  Before
going down to Ruggo's realm, she became a demilich.  So she had no
problems cleaning everything out.  The throne gave her a genocide, so
she eliminated master mind flayers from the game.  This had the
consequence that later in the lawful quest Mel C. was a vampire bat
instead of a master mind flayer.  The other Spice girls were still there
in their "natural" form, i.e. as mind flayers.  As it turned out, this
was to remain the only genocide of the game...

Two levels above, still in lich form, an elf lord zapped her with a wand
of draining - Boing!  He did not stand a chance.  She had some fun with
a pet chameleon that she saw turning into a pit bull when she saw it
first, so she immediately threw it a fortune cookie, in order not to
have a tough opponent.  It attacked the shop keepers in mine town
whenever it took on a mindless form such as a zombie or elemental form,
but never managed to kill one.  Later it was killed in the town of the
main dungeon by a watchman.

Up to the altar on Dlvl 1 with a wand of create monster.  Sacrificing a
few times finally yielded Mjollnir.

Now it seemed to me it was time to proceed downwards.  On Dlvl 9, she
found a wand.  Moving carefully into a hallway, she engraved with it:
"You may wish for an object!"  (Another novum for me: none of my
characters getting an early wand of wishing has died before.)  Why, two
blessed scrolls of charging.  But I did not want to take any chances.
Stashed the wand away until I would be able to determine its charges
(did not want to wrest out the last charge on the first attempt to zap
it), my character was strong enough for the time being.

One level deeper an altar to Tyr with a priest.  Well, that was very
good, I could now determine my scrolls of identify to be uncursed and
read one which revealed the wand to be at 0:1.  First wish:  blessed +2
deep dragon scale mail; recharge, second wish: blessed fireproof +2
cloak of magic resistance;  third wish, blessed fireproof +2 speed
boots.  (I was quick already, since I had reached level 9 in the
meantime.)  Now my valk had level drain resistance, magic resistance and
reflection.

Dlvl 11 was the kobold level.  This was the first time I had it
consisting of many interlaced rooms filling almost the entire level.
After cleaning it out, found a large box.  Opened it, there were two
wands in it, a wand of striking and a wand of wishing, this one at 0:3.
  I decided I was going to use up the first one wishing for an artifact.
  Looking up the artifact tables, I did not find Frost or Fire Brand
attractive enough although I was skilled in long sword.  Grayswandir or
the Bat from Hell seemed right.  I decided for the latter, since I had a
silver saber already and since it would do better damage early on.

It turned out to be a very nice weapon.  Proceeded to discover the three
quests from level 15 to 17, carefully avoiding the chaotic one.  I used
a ring of searching to find the protals and since the first two were
lawful and neutral, I did not even have to take the risk of entering
Vecna's level on Dlvl 17 (I was by no means ready to take on arch
lichs).  Somewhere Gwen had identified a scroll of enchant weapon and
blessed it, but it brought Mjollnir only to +1.

She then did the neutral quest immediately, because it is easy.  She
only started the lawful one, killing luckily all the giant ticks and
fleas before they could start multiplying, but retreated then for lack
of a means of levitation.

That was also a problem in Grund's stronghold.  And she had nothing for
the drawbridge.  But then a monster left a wand of striking.  She
decided to turn into a vampire and this way she managed to get across
the moat.  Always alert to retreat should a cockatrice turn up, she
cleaned out the stronghold and even killed Grund in vampire form, before
turning back to doppelganger form due to the time out.  Found the four
blessed potions of enlightenment which seem to be guaranteed there and
used a wand of cold to return across the moat.  She had also equipped
herself with an assault rifle and a few bullets here.

On Dlvl 14, she found the portal to Ludios and cleaned out everything
outside the fortress proper.  No food problems any more and many
bullets, some of which were enchanted to +4 soon. There she also got
disintegration resistance.  She did not need the gold, having already
gotten the message "Thy selfless generosity is deeply appreciated" from
the priest on Dlvl 10.

She had levitation boots, uncursed with holy water, so she could do the
lawful quest now.  She also had water walking boots, so she decided to
kill the eels too and look for some loot on the island.  There was a
statue of an arch lich.  It came alive!  (Never had done so before, but
I may have had genocided arch lichs in all cases I visited the island
before.)  This could already have been her demise, as she could not hit
him with her +0 Bat from Hell and all the +4 bullets were in her bag of
holding she had left outside the water area (having carried too much to
get through...).  Fortunately the +1 Mjollnir did hit the arch lich
(although without the lightning damage, I suppose - she wore a blindfold
because of a summoned umber hulk, so this was not quite clear, but when
trying to repeat the situation in wizmode later, the arch lich did not
take lightning damage from Mjollnir).  Still, without her wand of death,
allowing her to get rid of a dragon fast, she might have bitten the
dust.  After having killed the arch lich finally, she hastily retreated.

She made sure she would be admitted to the quest (in slashem you don't
seem to have to be level 14) but did not try it yet.  Before proceeding
further, she wished up a magic marker to improve her armor and to
enchant her Bat from Hell to +6.  Her AC was now -35 and she was pretty
confident.

The other side branches, such as Wyrm Caves and Spider Caves were
largely uneventful.   The Spider Caves provided two potions of
invulnerability.  She had discovered the black market, but did not yet
exploit it, cleaned out the nymphs level and hit the level with the
disgruntled adventurers.  Here the fact that she was level drain
resistant proved crucial.  Still there was much fighting and she was
paralyzed twice.  She went back (having teleport control and many cursed
scrolls of teleportation) to the lawful quest and finished it.  The mind
flayers were shot.  In their house, there was an amulet of flying, the
seocond time - I presume it is guaranteed.  Then Gwen teleported to Dlvl
2, where she used a toilet to make some more water and decided to do
some sacrificing on Dlvl 1.  Odin gave her another gift, a polished
shield named Mirrorbright.  This was exactly what she needed - she had
already contemplated wishing for a shield of reflection.  Now she
switched her amulet of reflection for one of flying.  No danger from
pools or lava anymore...

She cleaned out the out the Lost Tomb and felt it was time to do the
quest.  Surtur would not stand a chance against her.

Well, I still believe he would not have.  When arriving at his level, I
froze the lava around the staircase, so he would not drop anything in it
when he followed me to the staircase.  I wanted to wake him up and
teleport back there immediately.  When I approached his lair, I was
wondering: I thought there would be a drawbridge.  There seemed to be
none, just a hallway to walk in.  Well, some giants blocked the entrance
with boulders.  I opened my bag of holding, took out the wand of
striking and tried to destroy the boulders.  The drawbridge was
destroyed and Gwen who had actually stood on it, was hit by a piece of
it.  DYWYPI?  So there had been a drawbridge after all, and she had
stood in exactly the wrong square.  Had she moved one square back,
nothing would have happened to her.  Had she used her wand of digging
that was outside the bag to pulverize the boulder (yes that works in
slashem), I presume the drawbridge would have remained undestroyed.  Now
what I am wondering about: trying to recall my previous valkyrie
ascensions, it seems to me that the drawbridge had been up in at least
one case (this is more convenient, because if you know you are going to
destroy it, you are more careful, also it cannot be destroyed under your
feet by a fire giant with a wand of striking in that case).  What
determines whether it will be up or down?  Is this random?  (The castle
and Grund's drawbridge are always up.)

